<title>CANADA: Canadian Gas Association storage survey - Sept 13.</title>
<headline>Canadian Gas Association storage survey - Sept 13.</headline>
<dateline>CALGARY 1996-09-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canadian Gas Association (CGA) weekly survey of Canadian natural gas in storage in billion cubic feet (bcf):</p>
<p>							 Pct Full  Pct Full</p>
<p>		 09/13/96  09/06/96  Pct Full  Week Ago  Year Ago</p>
<p>East	    183.87    175.31    79.68	75.97     80.80</p>
<p>West	    222.26    214.06    80.39	77.93     88.80</p>
<p>Total Canada  406.13    389.37    80.06	77.03     84.80</p>
<p>East-West division is the Manitoba/Saskatchewan and North Dakota/Minnesota borders.</p>
<p>East capacity 09/13/96: 230.77 bcf, 09/06/96: 230.77 bcf.  </p>
<p>West capacity 09/13/96: 276.49 bcf, 09/06/96: 274.69 bcf.</p>
<p>The Canadian Gas Association survey includes liquefied petroleum gas, all Canadian operators of gas storage and Canadian companies contracting gas storage in the U.S. -- Reuters Calgary Bureau 403 531-1624</p>
